+Because the context is a fig tree and a mustard tree — and sym:sym-tree[trees] are another symbol that Scripture defines as kingdoms or nations. The phrase __“thrown into the sea”__ is a symbol clearly referring to Babylon the Great, as the link:/books/symbolic-language/the-fall-of-babylon/[Fall of Babylon] chapter demonstrated — and as the next chapter will trace from the Song of the Sea onward.
 
 What we learn from this is that the symbolic language of the Bible is interconnected: symbols are defined in terms of symbols and phrases, as well as the verbs, adjectives, and other personifications used with the symbol.
